§ `Regulations 43(4) and 44(3) as obligations with a deadline (MUST ... WITHIN 14): traces, read by hand`

-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with #ASSERT on the main binary, so these traces are READ, not asserted.  Expected from the text
-- ("within fourteen days"): notifying at time 14 or earlier is FULFILLED; at time 15, or never, is a BREACH.  The decision functions
-- above (`... was given within fourteen days`) are asserted with the same boundary.
#TRACE `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate` DOES `reg 43(4) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 14

#TRACE `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate` DOES `reg 43(4) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 15

#TRACE `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

#TRACE `reg 44(3) the trustees must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 44(3) the trustees of a relevant trust` DOES `reg 44(3) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 14

#TRACE `reg 44(3) the trustees must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 44(3) the trustees of a relevant trust` DOES `reg 44(3) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 15
